  "methods": {
    "lan": "Native DNS engine captured all 216 LAN cases directly against 127.0.0.1:5531 and [::1]:5531 on an isolated GitHub-hosted Ubuntu runner. The containers use public 0.5.1 image digests with amd64 selected by the runner. No system DNS or private-access publisher was selected.",
    "internet": "Configured system DNS at the observed 1.1.1.1:53 endpoint; operator confirmed the security intermediary disabled. Recursive observation, not direct authoritative or cache-free proof.",
    "additional_control": "Separate explicit public authoritative endpoint 108.162.192.65:53 for six public additional-data cases; not system DNS. Operator confirmed client disabled; socket destination alone does not exclude interception.",
    "publication": "Set each local_endpoint field to null and append a publication note. Preserve all DNS wire bytes, decoded records, remote endpoints, timings, events and run identity. Record original-capture and published-report SHA-256 hashes."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "The LAN reports cover 216 tests each. Eleven deliberate transport-fault cases retain network_error/inconclusive outcomes in both reports; two IPv6-only cases are unavailable in the IPv4 report.",
    "Capture through isolated runner loopback verifies fixture data and the engine capture path; it is not a product resolver, VPN or ZTNA baseline.",
    "Optional Additional data and policy rewrites require scenario interpretation; these captures do not make optional data a universal RFC MUST.",
    "DNS-behavior comparisons ignore documented run volatility and are not byte identity, TTL-policy approval, full RFC certification or product-baseline signoff."
  ],
